=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_7c2a — Baking items rest in pantry and drawer; the counter is for dinner cooking (fork of p_d1e6)

The parent document p_d1e6 predicted the baking tray, mixing bowl, spatula, and kitchen knife would be on the counter during Marco's weekday morning baking (06:50–09:00) and Yuki's weekend afternoon baking (13:00–16:00). The evidence has now refuted both windows: the mixing bowl and kitchen knife claims scored 3-against / 0-for on weekend afternoons, and the weekday morning window produced no counter sightings for any baking item (the tray was at pantry_shelf_k1 at 03:00 and 18:00; the spatula was in drawer_k_k1 at 03:00 and 18:00). The single 11:00 weekday counter sighting for the baking tray is an outlier, not a routine.

What changed: I removed the weekday 06:50–09:00 and weekend 13:00–16:00 counter windows for all baking items. The baking tray and mixing bowl now rest at pantry_shelf_k1 all day; the spatula and kitchen knife rest in drawer_k_k1 all day. I added an 18:00–20:30 dinner-cooking window where the spatula, kitchen knife, and pan appear on the counter (supported by 19:00 weekday sightings: spatula x3, knife x1, pan x2; and 18:00 weekend: spatula x2). The cutting board stays on the counter permanently (it is a fixture, seen there at 03:00, 18:00, and 19:00 on weekdays).

What would refute this fork: the baking tray or mixing bowl at counter_k1 at 07:30 on a weekday (it should be at pantry_shelf_k1); the spatula at counter_k1 at 10:00 on a weekday (it should be in the drawer); the kitchen knife at counter_k1 at 14:00 on a weekend (it should be in the drawer).

